  "notes": "So So Def's founder, and **one of the six multi-mode entries the volume declares**: its table lists him as entried here with a mode folded in from `crunk`, and states the switch outright — \"clap on 3 (snap) ↔ clap on 2&4 (R&B) — one switch moves him\". The two `modes` are therefore authored deliberately, replacing the parent's inherited moods, and each carries a harmony and melody delta as well as the backbeat switch, because a mode that differs only in feel is not a mode. He is tier `standard` rather than flagship for one structural reason, stated below: the research says his records often carry no separate bass voice at all, so this model has no `bassline` block and cannot declare the full five-part set a flagship owes. The base is the R&B side: 88–104 straight, mode 96. Three drum deltas describe what the research calls \"the leanest kit in the lane\" — \"a **programmed TR-808-styled kick and hi-hat** and nothing else… kick on 1 and the 8th before 3, an 'understated backbeat' on 3, 16th hats at low level, no snare fills\": syncopation 0.12, `lockTo808` 0.5, a hat lane at 0.18 fill density with a 0.24 velocity floor, and `fills` pushed to sixteen bars. \"**Handclap stacks are the signature layer across both modes**\", so the snare stacks clap and snap in the base and in each mode. Harmony is the sourced progression: `vi–V–iii–IV` (Am–G–Em–F) in **C major** — \"he is comfortable in major keys where the lane defaults minor\" — over \"a simple piano arrangement\", built from interpolation on 4-bar cycles. The low end is stated as an absence: \"808-derived kick doubling as the bass; a separate bass voice is often absent entirely\", so `drums.bass808` takes role `bassline` and there is deliberately **no** `bassline` block. \"Emotional restraint rather than technical vocal display\" is the 0.86 step share and the high chord-tone bias. ⚠ In snap mode the BPM is the research's own felt reading, \"70–82 half-time (= 140–164 notated)\". ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every velocity and density number and the 6:4 mode weighting — the research says the switch exists, not how much of the catalogue each half is. ⚠ `session.keys` is part-sourced: the entry names `C`, `Db`, and the remaining values `Fm`, `Abm`, together with all 4 weights, are INFERRED rather than read from the entry.",
